      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The original packs too much logic into single expressions: a nested `assertTrue` inside a lambda *and* a chained `.compareTo` on the result, making it hard to read at a glance. I'll improve it by:\n1. Extracting the lambda body into a named helper\n2. Breaking the chained assertion into named variables\n3. Splitting the two test scenarios so each is independently legibleThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the lambda body into a named block with a descriptive variable (`elapsed`, `checkTime`, `beforeCall`) and adds inline assertion messages, making each scenario's intent immediately clear without altering any runtime behaviour."
